    <string name="ludo_how_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="ludo_rule_1">Roll a 6 to bring a token out of your base. Every 6 gives you another roll; three 6s in a row lose your turn.</string>
    <string name="ludo_rule_2">Move a token clockwise by the number rolled. If only one move is possible it is made for you.</string>
    <string name="ludo_rule_3">Landing on an opponent sends their token back to its base and earns you another roll, unless it is on a safe square (the coloured start squares and the ★ squares).</string>
    <string name="ludo_rule_4">Capturing an opponent gives you another roll, just like a 6.</string>
    <string name="ludo_rule_5">Your own tokens can share a square. Tokens of different colours that share a safe square do not capture each other.</string>
    <string name="ludo_rule_6">After a full lap, turn into your coloured home column. You need the exact number to reach home.</string>
    <string name="ludo_rule_7">The first player to bring all four tokens home wins.</string>
